This function first attempts to fetch the status YAML from the feature branch using git, and if that fails, it falls back to reading from the local filesystem, returning an empty object if the file doesn't exist or can't be parsed. I'm realizing that in `escalateFeatureDrift`, the local filesystem is already synced to the feature branch after the checkout, so reading from there works fine—but the real problem is in the main `runFeatureReviewCycle` loop where `readStatusYaml` gets called before any branch switching happens. Let me check the test file to see what adjustments might be needed there.

